.UPDATE...
Issued at 950 AM PDT Wed Aug 5 2026

Solid marine layer this morning impacting the Bay Area and
Central Coast. As another forecaster in the office pointed out
this morning pretty impressive to see an over performing marine
layer deepen to nearly 1800 feet with anomalously high 500mb
heights. Not as much drizzle being reported this morning, but the
ample moisture in the low levels has led to mist. Above the marine
layer is a completely different story. High elevation sensors
showed another classic nocturnal drying event this morning.
Sensors showed humidity "recovery" to around 30 percent yesterday
evening then humidity values plummeted through sunrise as the
marine layer moved inland. This would definitely be a fire weather
concern, but fortunately winds are relatively light. Other item
of note this morning is some high level smoke being picked up by
satellite lurking over the coastal waters and potentially the
North Bay. Surface sensors are not showing it reaching the ground
as of now therefore it`s likely high level drift smoke.

For today - the over performing marine layer is bringing much
needed relief to the interior. No Heat Advisories are needed as
temperatures cool and HeatRisk concerns decreases. The marine
layer will slowly ease back to the coast, but linger for the day.

No update needed this morning.

Will be focusing on another round of heat later in the week and
developing near critical fire weather conditions.

